<article class="env-lemma" id="0932">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0932">Lemma <span data-tag="0932">18.27.8</span>.</a> Let $\mathcal{C}$ be a category, resp. a site Let $\mathcal{O} \to \mathcal{O}'$ be a map of presheaves, resp. sheaves of rings. Then </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}\nolimits _\mathcal {O}(\mathcal{G}, \mathcal{F}) = \mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}\nolimits _{\mathcal{O}'}(\mathcal{G}, \mathop{\mathcal{H}\! \mathit{om}}\nolimits _\mathcal {O}(\mathcal{O}', \mathcal{F}))  \]
</div>
  <p> for any $\mathcal{O}'$-module $\mathcal{G}$ and $\mathcal{O}$-module $\mathcal{F}$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This is the analogue of Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/08YP" data-tag="08YP">10.14.4</a>. The proof is the same, and is omitted. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>